# Deny by default: `COPY . ./` must receive only intended source, never whatever else happens to
# sit in a working copy (an .env, a certificate, an appsettings override, build output). Everything
# is excluded, then exactly the files the build needs are re-included — the re-includes match one
# path level (Sql/ excepted, re-included whole for the schema files), so nothing inside an
# excluded directory (obj/'s generated .cs included) comes back. A new source directory must be
# re-included here deliberately; that friction is the feature.
*
!LaPluma.CoreApi.csproj
!*.cs
!Sql/
